 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfzRa-GMTAF/",
 "title": "3R's Sales Ritual Framework",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains that instead of just focusing on high call volume when sales are down, salespeople should use a daily routine called the 3R framework. The main lesson is to focus on reviewing, reflecting, and rehearsing to improve 1% at a time rather than confusing busyness with closing deals.",
 "key_points": [
  "Do not just measure failure by increasing call volume (e.g., 200 calls, 50 follow-ups, 3 hours of call time).",
  "First R - Review: Pick one customer conversation from the day that is worth going through.",
  "Second R - Reflect: Identify one thing you could have done better, such as your introduction, asking more probing questions, or having a better understanding of your product.",
  "Third R - Rehearse: Practice a better response for the part where you could not answer the customer well.",
  "For the next 7 working days, spend 10 minutes answering three questions: What happened today? What could I have done better? What will I practice tomorrow?",
  "Small improvements make you better 1% at a time.",
  "Do not confuse being busy with making 200 calls; daily habits help shape what you can achieve next."
 ],
 "content": "Share it to someone who needs to use this 3R’S to be better at sales from tomorrow. Bro, my manager has told me to do 200 calls daily, create 50 follow-ups and reach three hours of call time because my sales are not happening. Who even does that, man? This is how most of the sales people measure when they're not able to close a deal. But very few take time to measure how can they improve themselves. Think about F1 driver Kimi Antoni, the world champion. The result we see on the track was only one part of his performance. And at the highest level, it comes with a daily ritual. So here's a simple framework. I call it as 3 R sales ritual, which I want you to try tomorrow as a salesperson. So if you're in sales, I want you to save this reel and follow so that you The first one is review. Pick one customer conversation from Which you feel worth to go through. Reflect. Identify one thing you could have Maybe your introduction, more probing questions to know him better, or better understanding on your product. Third is the rehearse. Practice a better response for the you couldn't answer him well. Now for the next seven working days, spend 10 minutes answering these What happened today? What could I have done better? What will I practice tomorrow? And that small improvement can make you better 1% at a time. So don't confuse being busy with making 200 calls. daily habits can help shape what you can achieve next. Send it to someone who can use this for Until then, your friendly neighborhood salesman.",
